  "findings": [
    "Taira's Torii closes a Connect socket on any text frame; the previous 20 s text keepalive ended every session. Keepalive is now a sequenced Connect Ping.",
    "The service called the global setTimeout/clearTimeout as methods; Chrome throws Illegal invocation, so connect() failed before attaching socket handlers (also true of the retired implementation). Found by the extension smoke, fixed with a regression test.",
    "The canonical checkout's node_modules had tiny-secp256k1 2.2.4 while yarn.lock pins 2.2.5, which fails the release head's new WASM provenance check (test-chrome-release-audit) with or without this branch; these results use an install that matches yarn.lock."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "SORA Nexus: NetworkId not pinned and minamoto.sora.org served a certificate for another hostname on 2026-11-21; Nexus links are refused.",
    "Raw requests: answered SIGNING_KEY_REQUIRED; no SDK can register the required off-chain signing key.",
    "Native instructions other than an asset transfer need the SDK's Rust decoder and are refused, not signed."
